##* {{RQ:Pope Essay on Man|epistle=IV|lines=191–193|page=71
|passage=You'll find, if once the Monarch acts the Monk, / Or Cobler-like, the Parſon vvill be drunk, / VVorth makes the man, and VVant of it the '''Fellovv'''; {{...}}}}
